  "result": "The test passes on the before snapshot and fails on the after snapshot, on `background-color expected rgb(37, 99, 235), got rgb(220, 38, 38)`.\n\nIt finds the \"Open an Account\" button by its selector outside any iframe. It then checks the four values from the before snapshot: background-color `rgb(37, 99, 235)`, padding-top and padding-bottom `12px`, and a height of 42px give or take 1px.\n\nThe prompt contradicts itself. The design intent describes the red, taller button as the change that was made, and rule 4 says not to assert on intended changes. But those two changes are the only thing that was flagged, and the test has to fail on the after snapshot. So I went with the regression report, which says this breaks the rule that blue marks primary actions, and asserted on both.",
